{
 "idea": {
  "id": "rev_resid@jp",
  "family": "reversal",
  "title": "Buy the week's losers and short its winners, after taking out the market and the sector",
  "why": "A stock pushed down by someone who needed to sell, with no news about the company, tends to come back once the selling stops; whoever takes the other side is paid for it. Taking out the market and sector move leaves the part most likely to be that kind of pressure. Known since Lehmann (1990) and Jegadeesh (1990); the open question is whether anything is left after costs in names liquid enough to trade.",
  "source": "Lehmann 1990; Jegadeesh 1990; Da, Liu, Schaumburg 2014 (residual reversal)",
